From fec967d8642ed9cc294db20e9949f51b23bf4b97 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: George Whewell <georgerw@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 02:28:33 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] media: coda: use two Coda980 reconstruction buffers

Coda980 reuses the Coda9 command ABI, but its Coda960 product-model
branch makes the H.264 encoder allocate four internal framebuffers. The
set-frame command already advertises two for this path, leaving the other
allocations unregistered with firmware.

The vendor Coda980 VPU API requires two normal H.264 buffers: the
reconstructed frame and its reference. It rejects a smaller registration,
retains the supplied count, and writes that count to CMD_SET_FRAME_BUF_NUM.

Select two internal buffers through the Coda980 ABI capability. Keep the
existing four-buffer Coda960 allocation unchanged.

Signed-off-by: George Whewell <georgerw@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/media/platform/chips-media/coda/coda-bit.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/chips-media/coda/coda-bit.c b/drivers/media/platform/chips-media/coda/coda-bit.c
index b648786c6..5ae013a56 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/chips-media/coda/coda-bit.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/chips-media/coda/coda-bit.c
@@ -1420,7 +1420,10 @@ static int coda_start_encoding(struct coda_ctx *ctx)
 	ctx->initialized = 1;
 
 	if (dst_fourcc != V4L2_PIX_FMT_JPEG) {
-		if (dev->devtype->product == CODA_960)
+		/* Coda980 uses two reconstruction buffers: current and reference. */
+		if (dev->devtype->has_coda980_h264_abi)
+			ctx->num_internal_frames = 2;
+		else if (dev->devtype->product == CODA_960)
 			ctx->num_internal_frames = 4;
 		else
 			ctx->num_internal_frames = 2;
-- 
